# Python backend

- Thin routers in `apps/api`; business logic in `core` / domain packages
- SQLAlchemy 2 mapped models; all schema changes via Alembic
- Prefer explicit Pydantic request/response models
- Injectable STT/LLM providers; tests use stubs
- Async only at I/O boundaries (Telegram, STT, LLM); keep DB session usage clear
- After behavior change: add/update pytest
- Do not introduce Redis, Celery, or microservices
